<h2 id="how-it-works">How it works</h2>
<ol class="docs__steps">
  <li><strong>Build.</strong> Build your project, and count your hours.</li>
  <li><strong>Ship.</strong> Ship your project to hit the boss with your hours, and get coins.</li>
  <li><strong>Get your prize.</strong> When the boss is defeated, collect your winnings, and claim a prize from the shop.</li>
</ol>
<p>In more detail: you sign in with your Hack Club account and connect Hackatime, which tracks the time you spend coding. You add a project and link it to a Hackatime project. When you have coded enough, you ship it. A staff member reviews the ship. Approved hours turn into coins, and the hours on your ship also hit the weekly boss. You spend coins in the shop.</p>

<h2 id="what-you-need">What you need</h2>
<ul class="docs__checks">
  <li>A Hack Club account. You sign in with it.</li>
  <li>To be a teen aged 13 to 18.</li>
  <li>Hackatime, connected. It is required, because it is how your hours count.</li>
  <li>A project, linked to a Hackatime project.</li>
  <li>A public GitHub link for your project when you ship it.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="sign-up">Signing up</h2>
<p>You sign in with your Hack Club account. Signing in with Hack Club gets you a free sticker.</p>
<p>Onboarding asks you for these things, and you can change your plan later:</p>
<ul>
  <li>The prize you want to work toward.</li>
  <li>What kind of project you want to build, and an idea if you have one. Nothing is locked in.</li>
  <li>Which days you want to code, what time works best, and how long you will code on those days.</li>
  <li>Your Hackatime account. It is required, because it is how your hours count.</li>
</ul>
<p>We remind you with a Slack DM on your coding days. No email or phone number is needed.</p>

<h2 id="eligibility">Who can join</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Any teen aged 13 to 18. You sign in with your Hack Club account.</li>
  <li>Battletown is free for teens, run by Hack Club.</li>
  <li>It runs for at least a month. We may extend it if it goes well.</li>
  <li>To spend coins, you verify your identity with Hack Club. If your account is not verified yet, your coins are saved for you.</li>
</ul>
